Statement of changes
--------------------

The copies here are NOT taken directly from the PrimeNumberTheoremAnd repository. They are
byte-identical to `src/latest/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd/` in

    https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs
    commit 8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e

which had already modified them relative to upstream PrimeNumberTheoremAnd. Neither the
upstream files nor plby's copies carry per-file copyright or license headers; the Apache-2.0
grant comes from the PrimeNumberTheoremAnd repository LICENSE.

Nature of the modifications, established by line-level comparison against
PrimeNumberTheoremAnd `main` and against the three most recent upstream commits touching
these files (94.6%, 97.1%, 91.7%, 95.7%, 81.4%, 100.0% and 100% of non-blank lines present
upstream, for Wiener, Consequences, Sobolev, Defs, Fourier, SmoothExistence and the three
Mathlib shims respectively):

  * content pruned to the fragment needed downstream;
  * `set_option linter.style.*` / `linter.flexible` suppressions added;
  * proofs repaired for a newer Mathlib, one of them annotated
    `-- The dominated-convergence proof below needs more heartbeats in Lean 4.32.`

No exact upstream base commit reproduces these files by hash, so the derivation cannot be
pinned more precisely than "PrimeNumberTheoremAnd, as adapted by plby/lean-proofs at
8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e". This package makes no further change to them:
their SHA-256 sums are recorded in `pinned-sources.json`'s sibling analysis
(`formalizations/jsp-000320-cyr/evidence/packaging-provenance.md`, §6.2) and they are
shipped verbatim.
